cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MMT or MMT-LID, please cite the published C3NLP 2023 paper. CITATION.bib preserves ACL Anthology's original BibTeX key."
type: dataset
title: "MMT: A Multilingual and Multi-Topic Indian Social Media Dataset"
authors:
  - family-names: Dalal
    given-names: Dwip
  - family-names: Srivastava
    given-names: Vivek
  - family-names: Singh
    given-names: Mayank
url: "https://github.com/dwipddalal/MMT"
abstract: "Samples from MMT, an Indian social media dataset for multilingual topic modeling and language identification, including code-mixed text. The paper describes a 1,755,145-tweet corpus with 13 topics and 63 subtopics, and the 5,346-tweet MMT-LID subset with human-annotated language labels. This repository contains samples rather than the full collection."
keywords:
  - multilingual NLP
  - Indian social media dataset
  - language identification
  - topic modeling
  - code-mixing
  - code-switching
  - Hinglish
  - Hindi-English
  - Twitter dataset
  - MMT-LID
